cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rafid or its results, please cite it as below."
repository-code: "https://github.com/zaidlatif2010/rafid"
title: "Rafid: running a 397B mixture-of-experts model on a laptop with expert streaming and cache-aware routing"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Zaid A. Lateef"
    family-names: "A. Kareem"
version: "0.8.4"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mixture of experts
  - LLM inference
  - expert offloading
  - SSD streaming
  - cache-aware routing
  - llama.cpp
abstract: >-
  Rafid is a C/C++ inference platform built on llama.cpp that runs mixture-of-experts language models
  far larger than RAM on consumer laptops. It streams experts from NVMe into a fixed RAM cache with a
  decayed-frequency policy, prefetches the next layer's experts with that layer's own router, reads the
  prompt while the user types, and offers graded cache-aware routing. It includes multi-turn
  conversation tests and a token-level fidelity test for approximate routing.
